# Append-only logs: keep every side's entries on a parallel merge instead of
# conflicting. `union` is a BUILT-IN git merge driver (no local config needed),
# so it is honored both by local git and by GitHub's server-side merge. Two
# PRs that each append a section to one of these files then merge with no
# conflict, keeping both. Scope this to append-only logs ONLY: union does not
# dedupe or reorder, so it must never guard a file where line order or
# uniqueness carries meaning.
ITERATION_LOG.md merge=union
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

